"entity": {
"name": "Andersons, Inc.",
"description": "Andersons, Inc. is a North American agriculture and renewable fuels company, which engages in the provision of railcar leasing and repair, turf products production, and consumer retailing. It operates through the following segments: Agribusiness, Renewables, and Other. The Agribusiness segment consists of commodity merchandising, the operation of terminal grain elevator facilities, and the manufacturing and distribution of plant nutrient products. The Renewables segment operates a merchandising portfolio of ethanol, ethanol co-products, and renewable feedstocks. The Others segment includes functions that provide support and services to the operating segments. The company was founded by Harold Anderson and Margaret Anderson in 1947 and is headquartered in Maumee, OH.",
